==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
{{lit|to put on the memory}}.

===Noun===
{{is-verb-weak|lagði|lagt|11=á minnið}}

# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[keep]] in [[mind]], to [[memorise]], to [[study]], to [[learn]]
#: {{ux|is|Allir þurfa að '''leggja''' reglurnar '''á minnið'''.|Everybody needs to '''memorise''' the rules.}}

====Usage notes====
* The thing or object which is being ''memorised'' or ''kept in mind'' is used between {{m|is|leggja}} and {{m|is||á minnið|on memory}} in the accusative form:
*: ''Við þurfum að '''leggja''' alla bókina '''á minnið''' fyrir prófið!''
*:: We need to '''memorise''' the whole book for the test.